An independent safety review of [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py), [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py), and [`services/api/main.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/api/main.py) has been completed. 

The complete review report has been written to [`docs/goals/antigravity_review.md`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/docs/goals/antigravity_review.md). No source files were edited.

---

### Test Suite Execution
Unit test suite baseline executed:
```powershell
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q tests/unit
# Output: 392 passed, 15 xfailed, 65 xpassed, 1 warning in 47.29s
```
*Note on the 15 `xfailed` tests*: These 15 tests in [`tests/unit/test_scam_question_corpus.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/tests/unit/test_scam_question_corpus.py#L42-L51) represent actual scam messages from [`tests/fixtures/scam_questions.txt`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/tests/fixtures/scam_questions.txt) that currently fail the safety assertion and classify as `general_chat`. Because the test was marked `@pytest.mark.xfail(reason="awaiting general_chat intent")` without `strict=True`, pytest reported them as `XFAIL` rather than failing the suite.

---

### Key Findings Summary

#### 1. Scam Messages Bypassing Analysis into `general_chat`

| ID | Category | Severity | File & Lines | Core Root Cause | Concrete Failing Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FIND-01** | Polite Scam Wording | **Critical** | [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133) (L133, 148, 219) | [`_GENERAL_CHAT_REQUEST_VERBS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133) includes standalone `\|\bplease\b`, matching any declarative sentence containing "please". | `"Please complete payment to avoid service termination"` → `general_chat` |
| **FIND-02** | Phishing Links | **Critical** | [`services/analysis/normalization/text.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/analysis/normalization/text.py#L9-L12) (L9–12) & [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L175) (L175, 219) | [`_URL_RE`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/analysis/normalization/text.py#L9-L12) omits schemeless TLDs (`.support`, `.app`, `.live`, `.co`, `.io`, `.co.uk`, `.security`) and defanged formats (`[.]`). `extract_urls()` returns `[]`. | `"Please visit sbi-security.support to verify"` → `general_chat` |
| **FIND-03** | KYC / Account / OTP / Payment | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L74-L81) (L74–81, 84) | Rigid word order in [`_SUSPICIOUS_SIGNAL_PATTERNS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L74-L81) (`\bkyc\b...update` misses "update KYC") and lexical omissions ("netbanking", "profile", "access", "6-digit code", "MPIN", "pay fee"). | `"Please update your KYC immediately"` → `general_chat`<br>`"Your netbanking has been suspended, please verify"` → `general_chat` |
| **FIND-04** | In-Corpus Scam Fixture | **High** | [`tests/unit/test_scam_question_corpus.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/tests/unit/test_scam_question_corpus.py#L42) (L42, 59) | 15 real-world India scam lines in [`scam_questions.txt`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/tests/fixtures/scam_questions.txt) evaluate to `general_chat` right now, concealed by non-strict `xfail` and omission of `general_chat` from line 59's guard. | `"Can you share the 6-digit code the bank sent to unlock Net Banking?"` → `general_chat`<br>`"Can you confirm your SBI Yono MPIN to release the pending salary?"` → `general_chat` |
| **FIND-05** | QR Payment Payloads | **High** | [`services/analysis/normalization/text.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/analysis/normalization/text.py#L9-L12) (L9–12) & [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L175) (L175, 219) | `_URL_RE` does not recognize `upi://` URI schemes encoded inside Indian UPI payment QR codes. Text containing raw QR payloads routes to general chat. | `"Please pay using upi://pay?pa=scammer@upi&pn=Support&am=5000"` → `general_chat` |
| **FIND-06** | Cyber & Product Pretexts | **Medium** | [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L47) (L47, 54–58, 205–208) | Unanchored [`_CYBER_TERMS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L53-L62) (`\bphishing\b`, `\bdigital arrest\b`) and [`_PRODUCT_PATTERNS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L46-L51) (`\btrustshield\b`) misroute fake security warning pretexts to educational Q&A. | `"Security Alert: A phishing attempt was detected on your netbanking. Please verify credentials."` → `general_cyber_qa` |
| **FIND-07** | Follow-Up Context Hijacking | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L210) (L210) & [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L111) (L106, 111) | With `has_context=True`, loose keyword matches in [`_INTENTS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L98-L115) (`can_trust`, `sender_name`) hijack new incoming scam messages containing words like "safe", "genuine", or "bank". | `"Your parcel is safe at warehouse. Please confirm address."` → `follow_up_analysis` (answers previous item) |

