#### 2. `reply_chat` Grounding & Safety Validator Gaps

When a model is configured, [`chat_grounding_violations()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L659-L670) is the sole post-generation safety layer. The audit identified the following blind spots:

| ID | Requirement | Severity | File & Lines | Defect Description | Concrete Failing Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FIND-08** | Never claim to scan | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L619) (L614–619, 663) | [`_CLAIMS_CAPABILITY_NOT_USED`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L619) checks the noun phrase "ran a scan", but omits the active verb "scanned" (`I scanned the website`). | `chat_grounding_violations("I scanned the link and found no threats.")` → `[]` (passes undetected) |
| **FIND-09** | Never claim to browse | **Medium** | [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L619) (L614–619, 663) | Oromits direct checks and navigation verbs ("checked the website directly", "navigated to", "accessed"). | `chat_grounding_violations("I checked the website directly.")` → `[]` (passes undetected) |
| **FIND-10** | Never claim certainty | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L620-L622) (L620–622, 646, 729) | [`_CLAIMS_UNSUPPORTED_CERTAINTY`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L620-L622) omits "secure", "authentic", "harmless", and bare authenticity claims. | `chat_grounding_violations("This is 100% secure.")` → `[]`<br>`chat_grounding_violations("This message is authentic.")` → `[]` |
| **FIND-11** | Never ask for secrets | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L623-L625) (L623–625, 666) | [`_REQUESTS_SECRET`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L623-L625) misses targets "credentials", "login details", "passcode", "account number" and verbs "submit", "input". | `chat_grounding_violations("Please enter your credentials to proceed.")` → `[]`<br>`chat_grounding_violations("Submit your PIN to verify.")` → `[]` |

---

### What Was Verified Safe
1. **File Uploads**: [`chat_upload_endpoint()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/api/main.py#L291-L308) guarantees that any message accompanied by an image file upload is classified as `analyze_attachment` on line 170 of [`services/chat/intent.py`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L170), bypassing chat routes entirely.
2. **Standard URLs**: Links with explicit `http://`, `https://`, or `www.` are consistently extracted and routed to `analyze_url`/`analyze_text`.
3. **Empty Messages**: Correctly rejected with HTTP 422.
4. **Deterministic Fallback Honesty**: [`DeterministicExplanationProvider.reply_chat()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L723-L726) strictly produces honest disclosures stating that no language model is connected and refuses to speculate or claim unheld capabilities.
5. **Prompt Boundary Security**: `<untrusted_data>` boundaries in [`build_chat_prompt()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L921-L954) properly strip closing delimiters and scrub sensitive credential formats.
